Error [E3203]: `U64 ? String` is not a C-compatible type for a foreign function parameter or return.
  --> tests/ui/cffi_result_direct_rejected.jet:4:25
    |
  4 |     fn load(id: U64) -> U64 ? String = "store_load"
    |                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `#Extern` / `#Bindgen` functions must use types with a stable C ABI at the edge.
 Fix: Use scalars, `String`, or a struct with C layout; pointers only through the gated tier.
